# Vivereply Concierge — environment template (production-grade).
# Production: set §1 in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables (Production scope). Local dev: copy to .env.local.
# NEVER commit real values: no .env* file belongs in git, and secret
# VALUES never travel over chat — names only. Every variable below is
# read by the code (audited); anything else is cruft.
#
# Shape of this file: §1 REQUIRED in production (blank = fill me),
# §2 recommended/optional tuning, §3 demo + seed (commented — needed
# only for the demo property), §4 terminal-only harnesses, §5 CI
# secrets, §6 things that live OUTSIDE .env entirely.

# === §1 REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION =======================================
# The app fails closed without these (login/chat/signup stop rather
# than run insecure). Fill every one before going live.

# Answering model: Muse Spark via the Meta Model API (primary, always).
# Key starts with LLM_, shown once — store it in a password manager.
META_API_KEY=
# Embeddings ONLY (answering stays Muse Spark): Google AI Studio key,
# gemini-embedding-001 at 768 dims. Chat grounding + knowledge seeder.
# (The Modal worker gets its COPY from Modal Secrets, not from here.)
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Database: Supabase Postgres via Prisma. DATABASE_URL = transaction
# pooler URI (port 6543, app at runtime). DIRECT_URL = direct URI
# (port 5432, migrations + `db push` via prisma.config.ts). Paste both
# from Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Database. Raw TCP must
# reach Supabase (sandboxed shells cannot — run db commands from an
# open machine).
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=
# Founder bootstrap login (super-admin). Checked first, so recovery is
# unconditional even if User rows break. Unset ADMIN_EMAIL disables
# the bootstrap (fail closed). Never reuse ADMIN_EMAIL for a User row
# (seed or signup) — the bootstrap shadows it. Recovery for a
# locked-out team is changing these.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Signs sessions + chat/widget/embed tokens (random, at least 16
# chars). Unset in production fails login AND chat closed — never a
# dev fallback there.
SESSION_SECRET=
# Encrypts per-property backend keys (AES-256-GCM, lib/secrets.ts).
# Random string, at least 32 chars. Without it, bindings cannot store
# keys and keyed backends fail closed.
# Rotation rule: safe to (re)generate ONLY while no bindings exist (an
# empty DB). Once a keyed binding is stored, changing this makes every
# stored secret unreadable — rotation then means re-entering each key.
BINDING_SECRET_KEY=
# Storage URL signing (server only): SUPABASE_URL + SERVICE key sign
# onboarding upload/download URLs — never the anon key, never the
# browser.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# App↔worker credential (random 32+ chars). The SAME value goes into
# the Modal Secret (§6) — the two are copies, not links.
WORKER_SHARED_SECRET=
# Verification emails (lib/email.ts). RESEND_FROM must be on a VERIFIED
# domain in production (DNS) — Resend's onboarding sender only reaches
# the account's own inbox.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM=
# Spam defense: Turnstile secret verifies human checks server-side;
# the public site key ships in the client bundle (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
# required). Signup fails CLOSED without the secret.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# Canonical app origin. REQUIRED for booking payments and recommended
# anyway: payment deep links are built ONLY from this, never from
# request headers. Production value: https://app.vivereply.com
APP_BASE_URL=

# === §2 RECOMMENDED / OPTIONAL (tuning + features) ===================
# All have safe code defaults; set only to change behavior. Uncomment
# what you use.

# Provider endpoint + agent model. Defaults work
# (https://api.meta.ai/v1, muse-spark-1.3); set only to point elsewhere.
# Free text by design (founder-only; procedure in docs/model-version.md
# — eval before deploy).
# META_API_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai/v1
# META_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3
# Sampling knob: 0-2, e.g. 0.2 for steadier tool-use. Unset = API
# default = today's behavior. Invalid values warn and behave as unset.
# Decided by eval runs, recorded in docs/decision-log.md.
# META_TEMPERATURE=
# Fallback backend: Baseten-hosted Muse Spark Open. Retried once, with
# the identical payload, when the Meta API errors (demo insurance).
# Inert when unset. The key works ONLY with
# meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026 (pinned in lib/meta.ts — no
# override). Guest text flows to Baseten on fallback turns.
# BASETEN_API_KEY=
# Deployed Modal webhook (ingestion worker). Without it, onboarding
# runs wait queued and /invoke retries later.
# MODAL_WORKER_URL=
# Per-tenant chat throttle: max turns per minute per property
# (DB-backed fixed windows; 429 + Retry-After past the cap).
# 0 disables (local dev).
# CHAT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN= (default 60)
# Per-IP second dimension: one address can't spend a whole property's
# budget. Same shape, same 429. 0 disables.
# CHAT_RATE_LIMIT_IP_PER_MIN= (default 30)

# --- Booking payments (OFF by default — suite users only) ---
# The chatbot insists on payment for held drafts and mints /pay/[token]
# deep links; guests pay via Stripe Checkout or manual transfer.
# Suite-only: fixture properties never get payment tools, even when on.
# PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY= (restricted key rk_…, test mode first; card method
#   appears in chat only when set — manual transfer always available)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET= (whsec_… from the webhook endpoint below)
# PAYMENT_LINK_TTL_HOURS= (default 24, max 72 — mirrors the hold window)
# MANUAL_PAYMENT_INSTRUCTIONS= (default text in lib/payments.ts; keep it
#   generic until per-property instructions ship — never a fake number)
# Stripe webhook endpoint to register (test mode, then live):
#   https://app.vivereply.com/api/pay/webhook  (event: checkout.session.completed)

# === §3 DEMO + SEED (commented — demo property only) =================
# A production tenant with its own binding row needs NONE of this.
# Uncomment only to serve the demo property (krishnachura-retreat).

# Fallback booking backend for the demo property (demo1 deployment).
# Properties WITH a binding row use their own URL and never read this.
# SUITE_API_BASE_URL=https://demo1.vivereply.com
# Slug of the demo property (matches its Property row + catalogue
# file). Code default is krishnachura-retreat; set only to rename it.
# DEMO_PROPERTY_ID=krishnachura-retreat
# NOTE: seed-tenant owner passwords live INLINE in
# prisma/seed-tenants.mjs (ownerPassword per entry) — there are no
# TENANT_PASSWORD_* env vars. Test tenants only; details plus the
# security contract in docs/seed-users.md. Rotate after prod seeding.

# === §4 TERMINAL ONLY (never Vercel) =================================
# `pnpm eval` logs in as the fixture owner and replays the cases
# against EVAL_BASE_URL. EVAL_PASSWORD is that owner's CURRENT password
# (docs/seed-users.md at seed time, or whatever it was changed to since).
# EVAL_EMAIL / EVAL_BASE_URL have defaults (sabreeze@test.com,
# https://app.vivereply.com); set only to point elsewhere, e.g. local dev.
# EVAL_EMAIL=
# EVAL_BASE_URL=
# EVAL_PASSWORD=
# `pnpm eval:dashboard` prices a window ONLY from these founder-pasted
# $/1M-token figures (no verified Muse Spark list price exists — never
# commit a guessed price here; pass them inline per run instead).
# COST_USD_PER_1M_PROMPT=
# COST_USD_PER_1M_COMPLETION=
# `pnpm probes` replays the 10 cross-tenant tests. A = mutating test
# tenant (seabreeze), B = read-only reference (krishnachura). A-owner id
# comes from SQL: SELECT id FROM "User" WHERE email='sabreeze@test.com';
# PROBE_BASE_URL= (default https://app.vivereply.com)
# PROBE_A_PROPERTY= (default seabreeze-test)
# PROBE_A_EMAIL= (default sabreeze@test.com)
# PROBE_A_PASSWORD=
# PROBE_A_KEY= (default test-seabreeze)
# PROBE_A_OWNER_ID=
# PROBE_B_PROPERTY= (default krishnachura-retreat)
# PROBE_B_EMAIL= (default krishnachura@test.com)
# PROBE_B_PASSWORD=
# PROBE_B_KEY= (default demo-krishnachura)
# PROBE_B_DOMAIN= (default demo1.vivereply.com)
# PROBE_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# PROBE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Cloudflare's documented Turnstile test keys (always pass, dev only):
#   site: 1x00000000000000000000AA / secret: 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# === §5 CI SECRETS (GitHub Secrets, NOT Vercel/.env) =================
# scripts/check-contracts.mjs reads these in CI (.github/workflows/
# nightly-contracts.yml). Set as repo secrets; for local runs, pass inline.
# SUITE_CONTRACT_ROOM_ID= (a stable room id on the Suite to probe)
# SUITE_API_KEY= (only if the backend requires one; empty = none)

# === §6 NOT .env (live elsewhere — listed so nothing is forgotten) ===
# --- Modal Secret `vivereply-onboarding` (Modal dashboard) ---
# The ingestion worker reads these from its Modal Secret, never from this
# repo's environment. Set via `modal secret create` (see worker/README.md):
#   APP_BASE_URL         public app URL (worker calls back here)
#   WORKER_SHARED_SECRET same value as §1 (both directions)
#   GEMINI_API_KEY       same embeddings key as §1
#   WORKER_DB_URL        least-privilege role URL (docs/worker-db-role.sql),
#                        NEVER the service key — the worker bypasses nothing
# Rotation rule: Modal values are COPIES, not links. Rotating
# WORKER_SHARED_SECRET or GEMINI_API_KEY in §1 means deleting +
# recreating the Modal Secret too, or app and worker silently disagree.
# No redeploy of the worker is needed afterwards (secrets resolve by
# name per run).
# --- Client dashboard variable (the CLIENT's server, not ours) ---
# Settings → Staff bridge codes reference CONCIERGE_BRIDGE_KEY as the
# conventional name for the bridge key on the CLIENT's server. It is
# minted in our Settings, shown once, and must never reach a browser.
# Nothing in this repo reads it.
